==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Living Legend''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Master of the Pacific '''at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Generally speaking, there is little point in deploying Mola King, as his attack power is mediocre, especially for his cost. He is effectively guaranteed to die in one hit from any attack, and lacks any form of special ability to offset his staggering weaknesses. His only redeeming traits are his range and recharge time, though considering how easily he dies, the player likely won't be able to stack him unless the enemy is well [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controlled]] or is short ranged.

His DPS is even lower than [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] (pre-True Forms), despite the fact that both of these units are free units who have far better survivability than Mola King. While Mola King may have a range advantage, there are a mere handful of enemies which outrange Bahamut and Ururun, but not Mola King, so this strength is unlikely to make a worthwhile difference in most stages.

Reconsidering Mola King from another perspective and asking: "Would he be good for beginners?" does not help him at all either. Despite his pathetic stats for an Uber Rare, Mola King still has the same cost as any other Uber Rare from the standard sets, making him as costly as any other Uber to upgrade, with none of the health or attack boosts that would be gained in light of equivalent exchange. It is recommended, especially for beginners, to give priority to certain [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] and [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]] cats when it comes to spending XP, as this unit only drains XP for little return, if invested in.

==='''True Form'''===
Master of the Pacific, despite improving the range considerably, ultimately changes little about his usefulness. As before, Master of the Pacific's DPS is only slightly higher than [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Schoolbus Nyandam]], who equals him in range, has more survivability and a chance to [[Slow|slow]] all enemies. Unless one really needs a unit with a lot of range, this True Form will not be worth the Epic Catfruit, which is better spent on most [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rares]] and [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] that are not this.

==='''Talents'''===
Master of the Pacific gains 3 talents, being Dodge, Mini-Surge, and Attack Up. All of them are very expensive and practically require each other to be effective. While still mediocre, they do improve the unit's utility somewhat.

'''Attack Up''' is a guaranteed talent to max out on, as Master of the Pacific gains up to 20% increase to his base damage. The '''Mini-Surge''' primarily serves to improve his DPS and extends his reach, as despite its very wide spawn area of 500~1,000 bringing inconsistencies, it will almost always spawn beyond the range of his own attacks, causing further havoc if it connects. As the Mini-Surge can hit up to 5 times, it can potentially even double Mola King's damage.

'''Dodge''' is very interesting, as it has a surprisingly high activation chance of 80%, though it only lasts for 1 second. Presumably used as a means to partially counteract the unit's extreme fragility, Dodge's inconsistency means it should not be actively relied upon, but rather serve as a last line of defense in case if something reaches him.

==='''Orbs'''===
An '''Attack Up''' orb is great if you have got the Mini-Surge talent, as an S-tier Attack Up orb will increase the Mini-Surge's total damage by a whopping 40K.

As for the trait of the orb, a '''Floating''' Attack Up orb is recommended because of the trait's abundance of backliners.

