==Trivia==
*Mola King directly evolves into Living Legend, as opposed to first evolving into Aquarium King as it would in ''Survive! Mola Mola''.
**This inconsistency is repeated once again, as the true form, Pacific Ocean King, isn't reachable by evolving from Living Legend, but from the Voyager, which is an entirely alternate evolution to the Living Legend. Once the player evolves from Aquarium King, he is asked what, as a Mola Mola, should be the most important thing in their life: Living Legend is reached by choosing "Blessings", but Voyager is reached by choosing "Freedom and Hope". The Living Legend, upon evolution, dies of old age, making the evolution sequence in The Battle Cats quite different from the one in Survive! Mola Mola!
*Its staggeringly low HP is a reference to the notorious fragility of [[Wikipedia:Ocean Sunfish|Ocean Sunfish]] (which itself is a running gag and main story driver of ''Survive! Mola Mola'' where the main objective is to avoid killing the sunfish).
*Master of the Pacific is the second ever unit to receive the Dodge Talent where it increases the chance instead of duration, the first being [[Nekoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Nekoluga]].

